    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0320" n="1054" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1054"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Neill to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lima,
                                Peru</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-09-13"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September 13, 1895</hi></date>. (Received
                        October 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 243.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the claim known as the
                    Hydrographic Commission of the Amazon, I have the honor to report I called the
                    attention of the new Government here to this long-pending case, as per copy of
                    note inclosed.</p>
                <p>I respectfully asked the new minister for foreign relations, Dr. Porras, to be so
                    kind as to present this case to the consideration of the Peruvian Congress, now
                    in session, that it might receive its early attention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard R. Neill.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d271-a1.xml" xpointer="d271-a1"/>
